<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>Utos.Workflow.Source</PackageId>
    <RootNamespace>Utos.Workflows.V1.Source</RootNamespace>
    <Description>Reads the Utos workflow source format — what authors write — and maps it onto utos.workflow.v1.Workflow, as specified by api/docs/workflow-source-format.md and api/docs/workflow-schemas.md. Shared so that every front end reads a document the same way: a workflow one tool accepts cannot be one another rejects. Reports defects as coded, path-addressed UTOS-S### issues.</Description>
    <PackageTags>utos;workflow;yaml;source;protobuf</PackageTags>

    <!--
      Enabled here and nowhere else in this repo. The other packages are generated protobuf, where
      the annotations would be the generator's to make; this is hand-written code that arrived
      from the CLI already written against it, and turning it off would delete real information
      about what a mapping may return.
    -->
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    The normative mapping, and the reason it is a package rather than a detail of the CLI: the
    hub's upload path reads the same documents, and two implementations of a mapping the spec
    calls normative is exactly what api/conformance/source/ exists to prevent. It lived in
    utos/cli until this package existed.

    YamlDotNet is the one dependency, and only its representation model is used — never the
    reflection-based object deserializer, which would not survive trimming in the NativeAOT `utos`
    binary that links this. That constraint is the CLI's, and it reaches here because the CLI is a
    consumer; see YamlJson.

    Deliberately NOT referenced: Utos.Workflow.Validation. Reading a document and judging a bundle
    are separate jobs with separate code ranges — UTOS-S### for a defect only a source document can
    have, UTOS-B/D/M/A/T/C/H### for one a bundle can. A caller that wants both references both.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Utos.Workflow\Utos.Workflow.csproj" />
    <PackageReference Include="YamlDotNet" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Utos.Workflow.Source.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- All source here is hand-written; EnableDefaultCompileItems=false (see Directory.Build.props). -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="**\*.cs" Exclude="bin\**\*.cs;obj\**\*.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\CHANGELOG.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="docs\" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
